# LaunchKit Core Rules

## Architecture
- This is a pnpm monorepo with Turborepo
- Main app: `apps/web` (Next.js 15, App Router)
- Database package: `packages/database` (Drizzle + Neon/pgvector)
- Storage package: `packages/storage` (multi-provider)
- Plugins package: `packages/plugins`
- RAG package: `packages/rag` (pgvector embeddings)
- Agents package: `packages/agents` (tool-calling framework)

## Critical rules
- Add `// @ts-nocheck` to any file that imports from `@launchkit/database` in the app
- NEVER import DB packages in client components (`"use client"`)
- ALWAYS check auth with `auth()` from `@clerk/nextjs/server` in API routes
- Use `getModel(modelId)` from `@/lib/ai` for all AI calls — never instantiate providers directly
- Add new public routes to `publicRoutes` in `apps/web/middleware.ts`

## Components
- Default to Server Components — only `"use client"` when you need hooks or browser APIs
- Use `shadcn/ui` components from `@/components/ui/`
- Icons: use `lucide-react` — never install icon packs
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v3 — no inline styles

## Code style
- TypeScript everywhere — avoid `any`, use proper types
- Named exports — no default export for components except pages
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class names
- Use `toast.success()` / `toast.error()` from sonner for user feedback
- API routes return `NextResponse.json({ data: ..., error: ... })`
